<title>SRI LANKA: Commercial up on growth outlook.</title>
<headline>Commercial up on growth outlook.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Good growth prospects pushed up Commercial Bank Ltd by 8.3 percent, or 10 rupees to 130 on turnover of 2,600 shares, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The share is rising because investors expect good growth in the second half,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>The scrip, a blue chip, fell to about 90 rupees on profit-taking after rising to around 120 rupees, following the market's mini rally earlier this month, he said.</p>
<p>Commercial Bank is one of four private commercial banks listed in Colombo.</p>
<p>--Prithi Kodagoda (941) 434319</p>
</text>
